WEBVTT

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
As I stand in the wind on a hill by a port town,

00:00.920 --> 00:07.592
minatomachi oka no ue kaze wo uke

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
mezurashii kurai atama wa karappo

00:07.656 --> 00:14.683
my head feels unusually empty.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
I was watching the town from the south side of the shore.

00:15.268 --> 00:21.940
haruka minami mukougishi de kono machi wo miteita

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
And so I sunk my unsteady passion into the depths of the sea.

00:21.965 --> 00:28.179
guratsuita jounetsu wo umi ni shizumeta

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
This surging power...

00:29.073 --> 00:34.745
tome donaku afureru chikara

00:29.073 --> 00:31.160
Black Jack

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
It's something hidden in everyone, everywhere.

00:36.247 --> 00:42.502
sonnamono wa darenimo dokonimo hisonde iru mono

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
Day after day, everyone tries their best.

00:43.296 --> 00:48.258
mainichi mainichi minna ganbaru

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
But people get annoyed when I mention it.

00:49.829 --> 00:57.184
sore wo ieba hito wa mina kemutagaru

00:57.685 --> 00:59.376
Oh FREEDOM

00:59.376 --> 01:01.369
will be there

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
It makes me glad...

01:01.389 --> 01:04.349
yokatta

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
That I found my place here.

01:04.594 --> 01:12.074
ibasho ga koko ni attakara

01:12.127 --> 01:13.645
Oh WISDOM

01:13.645 --> 01:15.494
will be there

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
I searched for the reason

01:15.522 --> 01:18.163
sagashita

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
why we can believe in the same air

01:18.164 --> 01:25.212
onaji kuuki shinjirarerukoto

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
as long as we're alive.

01:25.797 --> 01:32.677
ínochi aru kagiri

01:32.678 --> 01:34.763
He weaves the thread of life with his miraculous control of a scalpel.

01:34.847 --> 01:37.031
The genius surgeon who lives on a cape.

01:37.183 --> 01:39.794
His name is Black Jack.

01:51.868 --> 01:55.041
Originally "Younger Brother" by Tezuka Osamu

01:51.868 --> 01:55.041
Separated Brothers

02:18.228 --> 02:20.008
So, you're asking me

02:20.438 --> 02:22.523
to be your son.

02:22.524 --> 02:24.400
Yes. That's right.

02:24.734 --> 02:26.527
The contract would be for one year.

02:26.528 --> 02:30.114
We want you to live as Yokoyama Eizo's son.

02:31.700 --> 02:36.162
As a reward, we have prepared ¥20,000,000.

02:37.539 --> 02:40.040
See, Doc? Isn't it a good deal?

02:40.135 --> 02:42.626
You pretend to be this man's son,

02:42.627 --> 02:45.713
and we can buy a new set of pots and pans.

02:46.089 --> 02:48.174
Pinoco! You stay quiet.

02:49.676 --> 02:53.596
I was just thinking of making you a delicious curry.

02:54.139 --> 02:56.203
Why the hesitation?

02:56.349 --> 03:02.957
Even a man like you could have a great academic
record and a glorious resumé in an instant!

03:03.315 --> 03:05.733
On top of that, you can make money.

03:08.486 --> 03:10.571
Sorry, but I decline this offer.

03:12.157 --> 03:15.242
When I found a great job for you!

03:18.371 --> 03:19.622
W-Why?!

03:20.207 --> 03:23.422
First: I'm a doctor, not an actor.

03:23.668 --> 03:26.337
Well, of course.

03:26.671 --> 03:30.925
Second: I have no interest in an
academic record or a resume.

03:32.225 --> 03:35.846
Third: You're hiding something.

03:37.704 --> 03:38.497
Those are my reasons.

03:38.797 --> 03:40.157
Let's go, Pinoco.

03:40.185 --> 03:41.644
Wait up, Doc!

03:42.103 --> 03:43.187
Please wait!

03:47.275 --> 03:50.361
My older brother has cancer.

03:52.572 --> 03:56.367
He doesn't have much time left. He's at his end.

03:57.160 --> 03:59.136
Then hire me as a doctor.

03:59.746 --> 04:02.665
It won't work if I introduce you as a doctor.

04:03.416 --> 04:06.123
He's a very stubborn man.

04:06.628 --> 04:12.542
He probably won't accept an operation
from anyone except my son.

04:14.386 --> 04:16.971
So there were reasons behind this.

04:18.098 --> 04:20.599
Please! I beg you!

04:24.625 --> 04:25.865
New pots...

04:26.305 --> 04:27.998
Please, Doc.

04:31.111 --> 04:35.172
With medical exams, surgery, acting,
and other costs included,

04:35.699 --> 04:37.700
the cost will be ¥70,000,000.

04:37.953 --> 04:39.410
T-Then...

04:39.953 --> 04:41.492
You better thank Pinoco.

04:41.788 --> 04:44.248
I love you, Doc!

04:44.249 --> 04:46.652
I'll cook my best stuff!

04:44.916 --> 04:46.652
Hey now, Pinoco.

04:48.878 --> 04:52.113
But I make no guarantee regarding how well I can act.

05:00.307 --> 05:01.805
Where are we going?

05:02.058 --> 05:03.934
To my brother's house.

05:15.447 --> 05:18.365
Nee-san, it's been such a long time.

05:18.825 --> 05:20.485
Eizo, it's really you!

05:20.785 --> 05:23.579
Dear! We have a surprise guest!

05:25.707 --> 05:28.751
Nee-san, how's my brother's condition?

05:29.252 --> 05:31.681
Not very good.

05:35.938 --> 05:36.978
Is that Eizo?

05:37.085 --> 05:38.647
Why did you come here?

05:39.298 --> 05:40.658
What do you mean?

05:40.792 --> 05:43.419
He came to see you.

05:43.892 --> 05:47.770
Brother, I heard you weren't feeling well, so...

05:48.065 --> 05:50.814
It's none of your business.

05:50.815 --> 05:51.732
Brother!

05:52.233 --> 05:56.056
You knew this eventually happen!

05:56.363 --> 05:59.239
Dear, don't talk so loudly.

05:59.240 --> 06:01.867
Getting upset isn't good for you.

06:02.035 --> 06:02.993
Quiet:!

06:04.371 --> 06:06.038
See what I mean?

06:09.918 --> 06:13.212
Out in the gentle sunlight,

06:13.213 --> 06:18.050
I wish on the playful clover...

06:20.220 --> 06:22.426
Why do you have to go through all this?

06:22.931 --> 06:27.559
Perhaps you should know the story behind this.

06:29.187 --> 06:33.260
I'll tell you everything I know.

06:36.653 --> 06:39.388
Don't tell me you forgot.

06:41.449 --> 06:45.571
It happened when Dad fell ill from cancer.

06:48.441 --> 06:51.521
Yokoyama Printing Press

06:52.544 --> 06:55.142
What did Dad say before he died?

06:55.755 --> 06:57.756
Dad, come back to us.

06:57.757 --> 06:58.841
Dad.

07:00.510 --> 07:04.209
Boys, there's nothing we can do about this.

07:04.764 --> 07:09.435
Your great-grandfather and grandfather
also died from cancer.

07:10.061 --> 07:13.814
I knew that I have cancer too.

07:16.860 --> 07:19.823
We're all prone to cancer,

07:20.238 --> 07:24.158
You be careful of cancer too.

07:24.534 --> 07:25.836
Dad!

07:26.119 --> 07:30.873
Find a doctor who can treat you before you get cancer.

07:31.059 --> 07:34.585
Dad, I'll become a doctor who can treat cancer.

07:34.586 --> 07:36.336
I'll be a doctor too!

07:40.800 --> 07:42.308
Dad!

07:44.721 --> 07:49.210
Dad said that and died soon after,
leaving the two of us behind.

07:50.268 --> 07:55.909
Eizo, I have to take over Dad's factory.

07:56.107 --> 07:57.870
I'll work hard.

07:58.193 --> 08:01.528
I promise you won't have a hard time,

08:02.655 --> 08:04.948
SO you can become a doctor.

08:04.949 --> 08:06.325
Me?

08:06.326 --> 08:10.775
So you keep the promise we made with Dad.

08:13.333 --> 08:16.543
Okay! Then I'll become a doctor!

08:17.212 --> 08:18.473
It's a promise.

08:18.713 --> 08:20.258
Yeah, a promise.

08:27.399 --> 08:29.698
And you...

08:29.807 --> 08:31.683
I never forgot that promise!

08:37.815 --> 08:39.274
That's a wonderful story.

08:39.275 --> 08:40.859
It moved my heart!

08:41.402 --> 08:42.712
But I still don't understand.

08:42.987 --> 08:46.323
How does him becoming a doctor
relate to me becoming his son?

08:47.033 --> 08:49.928
This is his atonement.

08:55.625 --> 08:59.419
You were just about the worst in school.

09:00.046 --> 09:03.246
On every test, you came within
a hair's breadth of scoring zero.

09:03.550 --> 09:07.362
Whenever it was your turn to speak,
you became the laughingstock of the classroom.

09:07.720 --> 09:10.541
I did most of the homework for you.

09:12.267 --> 09:16.895
Every time I heard anyone badmouth you,
I paid them back.

09:17.480 --> 09:20.662
I protected you the best I could.

09:22.110 --> 09:27.734
You were close to flunking, so I walked
you to a cram school in a nearby town.

09:28.157 --> 09:30.409
It was dark by the time we walked home.

09:31.828 --> 09:35.831
Brother, my teacher told us to bring lunch money.

09:35.832 --> 09:40.127
Yeah, I'll pay it as soon as I get paid for this job.

09:40.128 --> 09:46.091
Every day, I managed Dad's factory,

09:46.092 --> 09:49.035
working hard, so you wouldn't have to.

09:56.185 --> 10:02.276
But as you grew older, you became even dumber!

10:02.567 --> 10:06.403
You only graduated from junior high
because the teachers were merciful.

10:06.512 --> 10:08.780
Make Eizo a doctor?

10:08.913 --> 10:09.800
Yes.

10:09.824 --> 10:11.783
I'm not sure about that.

10:11.784 --> 10:13.850
It costs a lot to become a doctor.

10:14.037 --> 10:18.081
It might be possible for you, but with Eizo's test scores...

10:18.458 --> 10:21.918
I swore to Dad that I'd make him a doctor.

10:22.092 --> 10:24.122
Please help me out!

10:24.380 --> 10:26.340
Please, teacher!

10:28.968 --> 10:31.320
I did everything I could,

10:32.472 --> 10:33.557
but...

10:37.894 --> 10:41.563
Jeez, why didn't he study more?

10:41.564 --> 10:43.869
That poor brother.

10:44.442 --> 10:47.152
It's not that he couldn't study.

10:47.427 --> 10:50.588
In his case, it wasn't the academics, but...

10:51.366 --> 10:52.574
But?

10:53.660 --> 10:55.626
His brother's great expectations?

10:56.037 --> 10:57.053
Yes.

10:57.622 --> 11:00.943
All the pressure must have hindered his performance.

11:01.918 --> 11:06.194
No matter how simply things were explained,
no matter how many extra lessons he took,

11:06.839 --> 11:10.342
and even with help from a private tutor, it was all in vain.

11:12.470 --> 11:16.264
Sweet talk, praise, encouragement,
inspirational speeches—

11:16.265 --> 11:17.823
Nothing led to results.

11:20.311 --> 11:24.902
Perhaps he refused to become a doctor subconsciously.

11:25.233 --> 11:31.133
Maybe he thought that his brother would give
up if he couldn't go to a medical school.

11:31.698 --> 11:32.948
Why do you think that?

11:33.267 --> 11:38.161
He's the man who built our IT firm from the ground up.

11:38.830 --> 11:43.897
I believe no ordinary man could ever build a company
that employs over a thousand people.

11:47.755 --> 11:49.297
I'm so bored.

11:49.298 --> 11:52.301
How much longer is that dumb president
going to make us wait?

11:52.593 --> 11:56.888
I want to cook with my new set of pots soon.

11:57.223 --> 12:03.645
Curry and rice, omelette rice, spaghetti,
beef stew, hamburger, pancakes...

12:04.105 --> 12:08.400
I'll make so much of everything you like.

12:11.821 --> 12:16.783
I was trying to make you a doctor,
no matter how many sacrifices I had to make.

12:16.784 --> 12:19.244
Didn't you realize how hard I worked?!

12:21.539 --> 12:22.748
I did.

12:24.542 --> 12:25.656
That's why

12:26.335 --> 12:33.066
I was so shocked when you bribed the academic
dean to force me into medical school.

12:33.509 --> 12:35.469
No! I don't want to be a doctor!

12:35.470 --> 12:37.220
I'm scared of shots!

12:37.221 --> 12:39.556
You're not getting the shots!

12:39.557 --> 12:41.349
Looks good!

12:41.350 --> 12:43.351
You look like a real doctor.

12:43.352 --> 12:46.649
I couldn't stand to see you act that way anymore,

12:46.898 --> 12:50.150
so I decided to run away from you.

12:46.931 --> 12:50.150
Eiichi, it's easier to die than try to become a doctor. So, I'm going to quit
and find a way to make ends meet. I'm very sorry, but I'm leaving.
Goodbye.

12:52.487 --> 12:54.154
Idiot!

13:04.123 --> 13:05.582
Idiot!

13:05.583 --> 13:07.459
Ohmigewdness!

13:08.377 --> 13:12.547
One sacrificed his own life and was betrayed
by the man to whom he entrusted his dream.

13:12.863 --> 13:19.317
The other could not stand up to the pressure
of being forced into a life of medicine.

13:20.264 --> 13:24.810
If they could care more about each other
and talk about their true feelings,

13:24.811 --> 13:27.270
I think this could have been avoided.

13:29.607 --> 13:32.734
The president seems to have been thinking
about this the whole time.

13:33.528 --> 13:35.487
That's why he made his son...

13:38.991 --> 13:42.770
For a while, I had no idea where you were.

13:43.287 --> 13:45.539
I cursed your worthlessness

13:45.540 --> 13:51.143
and kept this modest family business.

13:52.630 --> 13:55.423
It was many years after that...

13:57.301 --> 13:59.135
I was quite shocked.

13:59.387 --> 14:03.390
You'd become the president of a large company.

14:03.391 --> 14:07.809
On top of that, it was some IT-whatever
thing that was endangering my business.

14:13.192 --> 14:19.114
Soon after that, you came to visit
me and shamelessly asked me...

14:19.615 --> 14:23.785
Brother, let's work together from now on.

14:23.786 --> 14:26.830
You hadn't done enough by betraying me,

14:26.831 --> 14:29.213
so you tried to take over my business.

14:29.667 --> 14:32.711
Brother, I didn't mean it that way...

14:33.170 --> 14:35.255
I'll refuse no matter how many times you ask!

14:35.256 --> 14:39.092
I'll protect Dad's factory even if I die!

14:39.552 --> 14:42.974
Brother, I didn't come here about that.

14:43.514 --> 14:44.350
What?

14:46.767 --> 14:49.686
Please have an operation.

14:50.646 --> 14:51.855
Enough nonsense!

14:51.856 --> 14:55.041
I don't want to hear that from you!

14:55.818 --> 15:00.822
How dare you say that after betraying me?

15:00.823 --> 15:03.950
I just heard that you'd fallen ill, so...

15:03.951 --> 15:05.201
So what?

15:05.202 --> 15:08.538
What can you do when you're not a doctor?

15:10.382 --> 15:11.382
So...

15:11.918 --> 15:14.502
You brought a doctor who can treat me?

15:15.254 --> 15:16.386
I refuse.

15:16.672 --> 15:20.467
I'll never see a doctor you found.

15:23.012 --> 15:24.607
Is that all you've got to say?

15:24.847 --> 15:27.515
Then leave this place right now.

15:28.225 --> 15:31.394
It's true that I couldn't become a doctor,

15:32.605 --> 15:35.899
but I made my son become a doctor.

15:36.817 --> 15:37.817
What?

15:38.402 --> 15:43.642
I wanted to help out somehow, so I sent my son,
Eiji, to study abroad in America.

15:44.283 --> 15:46.034
And he just returned!

15:47.944 --> 15:50.413
He's become a great doctor.

15:50.414 --> 15:52.173
He's your nephew.

15:52.667 --> 15:55.835
Please let him see you!

15:56.337 --> 15:59.130
You made your son become a doctor?

15:59.632 --> 16:02.503
Yes! I think he can treat you.

16:02.969 --> 16:04.511
So, Brother...!

16:08.015 --> 16:11.476
I'm sure your son turned out to be a quack.

16:15.481 --> 16:16.773
Do whatever you want.

16:18.943 --> 16:19.943
Brother!

16:20.653 --> 16:22.362
Dear.

16:28.953 --> 16:31.287
Doctor, everything worked out.

16:31.288 --> 16:32.797
So please...

16:33.207 --> 16:35.000
I can't do it right now.

16:35.001 --> 16:36.167
I must take care of my own business too.

16:36.168 --> 16:37.437
B-But...

16:38.337 --> 16:41.586
I also need to practice pretending to be your son.

16:42.049 --> 16:43.074
Well...

16:44.010 --> 16:45.286
In a week.

16:45.761 --> 16:48.096
I need at least a week.

16:48.097 --> 16:49.723
What are you talking about?

16:49.724 --> 16:52.350
His condition is time-critical!

16:52.977 --> 16:54.649
Then try someone else.

16:55.354 --> 16:57.313
I don't care either way.

16:59.817 --> 17:01.276
All right.

17:13.503 --> 17:14.211
All right.

17:14.498 --> 17:15.541
You're sure about this?

17:15.833 --> 17:16.785
Where is he?

17:17.697 --> 17:18.410
I see.

17:19.530 --> 17:20.236
Thank you.

17:22.006 --> 17:23.457
Pinoco, we're going out.

17:23.674 --> 17:25.300
Okay!

17:25.342 --> 17:27.177
Aye-aye!

18:09.386 --> 18:12.443
Is this where he'll treat me?

18:12.681 --> 18:14.140
It is, Brother.

18:17.812 --> 18:19.354
And this is my...

18:19.540 --> 18:22.065
Is that Dr. Black Jack or something?

18:25.069 --> 18:27.333
How dare you try to trick me!

18:28.155 --> 18:30.615
Did you really think you could trick me?

18:33.786 --> 18:36.122
Sorry, but I looked into this a little.

18:36.580 --> 18:40.850
It's true that you have a son studying in America,

18:41.585 --> 18:45.803
he's still wet behind the ears
can't possibly treat cancer.

18:46.090 --> 18:48.728
B-Brother...

18:49.093 --> 18:54.148
So you asked him to be your son, huh?

18:55.641 --> 18:57.248
I didn't have any other choice!

18:57.768 --> 18:59.769
If I didn't do this, you wouldn't...

19:00.771 --> 19:03.647
I'll have nothing to do with your fake son!

19:04.066 --> 19:06.335
But I want to save you!

19:06.569 --> 19:09.592
But you said you'd let your son operate on me!

19:10.281 --> 19:11.858
Your real son!

19:16.662 --> 19:18.089
That's right.

19:18.372 --> 19:21.332
I am not Eizo-san's son.

19:23.085 --> 19:26.173
But, Eiichi-san, you clearly stated

19:26.755 --> 19:29.591
that you would let his real son operate on you.

19:30.259 --> 19:32.389
So what if I said that?

19:32.803 --> 19:34.554
Then the situation is simple.

19:36.473 --> 19:38.853
Let's have his son operate on you.

19:49.403 --> 19:51.362
E-Eiji, why...

19:51.363 --> 19:54.324
Are you Eizo's...

19:54.909 --> 19:57.380
I'm sorry to have kept this secret from you, Dad.

19:57.620 --> 19:59.494
I returned yesterday.

19:59.747 --> 20:03.416
I heard the story from your administrative assistant,

20:03.417 --> 20:06.415
so I flew to America on my own.

20:08.380 --> 20:11.049
Eiji-kun had difficulty making up his mind.

20:11.675 --> 20:17.347
Dr. Black Jack told me that he would support
me 100%, so I decided to do this.

20:20.309 --> 20:21.559
Eiji!

20:22.728 --> 20:24.736
Dad, let me make this clear:

20:25.189 --> 20:27.232
I became a doctor of my own free will.

20:27.816 --> 20:29.150
Eiji...

20:29.818 --> 20:32.497
Don't worry. I guarantee that I'll save Uncle.

20:32.988 --> 20:37.822
So, Dad, you don't need to worry about your past.

20:45.084 --> 20:48.503
Brothers are so wonderful.

20:50.089 --> 20:51.945
Do you still have a problem?

20:53.801 --> 20:58.104
Eiji better be the primary physician,
with you acting only as his assistant.

20:58.555 --> 20:59.514
Is that clear?

21:01.267 --> 21:02.338
We know.

21:03.560 --> 21:05.061
Take the patient to the operating room.

21:05.062 --> 21:07.063
Aye-aye!

21:12.236 --> 21:13.549
Hang on.

21:14.863 --> 21:15.738
Eizo.

21:16.448 --> 21:18.032
Yes, Brother?

21:18.742 --> 21:20.201
I have a favor to ask.

21:22.037 --> 21:28.242
Would you go visit Dad's grave with me once I get better?

21:32.756 --> 21:35.047
It's a promise.

21:38.345 --> 21:39.721
Yeah.

22:10.544 --> 22:17.550
I want to capture your heart with my silly smile.

22:10.544 --> 22:17.550
itazura no hohemi de muchuu ni sasetaino

22:17.551 --> 22:24.723
Only look straight at me.

22:17.551 --> 22:24.723
massugu na kimi no me ni watashi wo utsushitene

22:24.768 --> 22:32.025
Being kind isn't good enough.

22:24.768 --> 22:32.025
yasashii dake dewa nanika tarinaino

22:32.026 --> 22:42.535
I want to get in touch with your true heart, deep
within the you that nobody else sees.

22:32.026 --> 22:42.535
dare nimo misenai kokoro no oku no sotto furetai

22:42.536 --> 22:47.916
Being in the gentle sunlight,

22:42.536 --> 22:47.916
yawaraka na hizashi abite

22:47.917 --> 22:57.300
I wish on the clover that plays the melody of dreams,

22:47.917 --> 22:53.122
yume wo kanaderu clover

22:53.577 --> 22:57.301
kaze ni negai wo nosete

22:57.301 --> 23:08.061
and I search for a ray of hope beyond the blue skies,

22:57.301 --> 23:08.061
aoi sora no mukou e kibou no hikari sagasuno

23:08.062 --> 23:13.149
because I want to stay by your side forever.

23:08.062 --> 23:13.149
zutto soba ni itakara

23:13.150 --> 23:26.120
